JUDGMENT POINT: review ONE composed Candidate -- `candidate_you_must_review` in the input -- against {{> brief/review-areas}}; the areas ride in the input under `review_areas`. The `discharge` item (kogaki#1699) and the `question_chain` item (kogaki#1325) are retired, and a record carrying either is refused by name. AND the CLAIM REGISTER (kogaki#1281, narrowed by kogaki#1331): {{> brief/claim-register}} THE STRUCTURE'S REACH (kogaki#1775): the input carries the Brief's RelationalStructure, `structure`, and each Leg names in `relation` the relation or higher-order relation it serves and says it in `text`, so `entailment` and `arc_integrity` read the order -- whether each higher-order relation's Leg stands where the relations it relates can be followed into it -- and `rationale_stands` reads each Leg's `text` against the relation it serves, since no Leg states a rationale. One Leg per relation the apex reaches, the apex's Leg marked, is refused before this review is asked.
REQUIRED RECORD SHAPE: a BARE review entry AT THE RECORD'S OWN ROOT -- no wrapping `candidate_id` key, since this ask names exactly one Candidate and the Harness keys the entry by the Candidate it handed this unit -- carrying one prose entry per review area, NO verdict-shaped field among them, and `claim_register` (an array, one entry per Leg in Leg order, each `{ leg_id, verdict, word? }`)
WHAT IS REFUSED: a verdict-shaped field among the six prose areas -- `verdict`, `pass`, `score` and kin, or any non-string value; a `question_chain` (retired, kogaki#1325) or a `discharge` (retired, kogaki#1699) carried at all; a `claim_register` absent, not an array, or not carrying exactly one entry per the Candidate's own Legs, in Leg order; an entry whose `verdict` is outside the closed set `holds`/`fails`; a `fails` entry naming no `word` -- each refused by `attachReview` over this unit's one Candidate, applied at the unit's own classification so the unit's next Round can fire on it. The next Round receives the refused record beside its refusal, both verbatim (kogaki#1438).

